WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.708
What viral moment in Mission: Impossible — Fallout
was totally improvised?

00:00:04.708 --> 00:00:06.885
And how did the director react?

00:00:06.947 --> 00:00:11.180
Henry Cavill is well known for his devotion
to each role he takes on.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:15.400
Whether it's being faster than a speeding
bullet as Superman to grumbling his way through

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.650
a fantasy world as Geralt of Rivia on The
Witcher, he knows how to give his all in every

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:24.870
role and genuinely applies himself to every
single part he accepts.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:29.949
In Mission: Impossible — Fallout, the actor
took on the character of August Walker, a

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:34.306
CIA hire tasked with keeping an eye on the
entire Impossible Missions Force through their

00:00:34.306 --> 00:00:35.829
Special Activities Division.

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:40.550
That puts Walker on a collision course with
death-defying Ethan Hunt, a member of the

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:45.215
IMF and head of a globetrotting, tech-loving
unit of misfits and rogues.

00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:47.354
"You're not getting rid of me that easily,
Hunt."

00:00:47.391 --> 00:00:48.403
"That's not what this is about."

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.530
After a film filled with derring-do, the two
men fight it out via a helicopter duel, then

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.030
battle to the death on the edge of a cliff.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.149
Naturally, it's Walker who meets his maker
instead of Hunt.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:04.220
While Walker chases Hunt up the sheer side
of the rock formation, he's smashed in the

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.360
eye with some of the rigging attached to one
of the disabled helicopters when it comes

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.030
unmoored from the rockface.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:15.210
He falls into the explosion caused by the
now-dislodged helicopter as it hits the ground,

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.259
leaving Hunt to scramble to safety.

00:01:17.259 --> 00:01:22.020
There's another, more iconic moment Cavill's
character took part in — one that he admits

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.369
he's seen discussed multiple times on Reddit
— and you may not be surprised to learn

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:28.880
that he improvised that bit of onscreen action.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.869
It turns out his sense of humility and his
wicked sense of humor were both factors in

00:01:33.869 --> 00:01:35.740
birthing the moment to life.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.778
Here's what he says about the iconic moment
he improvised during a very memorable fight scene.

00:01:40.778 --> 00:01:44.710
During the film, Hunt and Walker are involved
in a bathroom brawl.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:49.670
As Walker approaches his opponent, he seems
to be pumping his arms, "reloading" his biceps

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.130
as if they were guns.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.621
The moment became something of an online meme.

00:01:53.621 --> 00:01:57.919
[sounds of fighting]

00:01:57.919 --> 00:02:04.091
During an October 2022 appearance on the podcast
Happy Sad Confused, Cavill admitted that the

00:02:04.091 --> 00:02:08.580
moment was an unscripted improvisation he
came up with off the cuff, saying.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:27.400
"The connective tendons in my biceps were
getting sore, so I had to warm them up before

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:31.030
I threw punches, and I'd literally do that
to warm them up."

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.734
He added in the podcast,

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:45.430
To Cavill's surprise, the director didn't
seem to have a problem with the gesture.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:46.430
Cavill said,

00:02:54.198 --> 00:02:56.370
"He said, 'Yes, definitely do that, do that.'

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.806
And so, and so we did."

00:02:57.806 --> 00:03:01.629
Henry Cavill is no stranger to thinking on
the fly while on set.

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:06.700
He told Digital Spy ahead of the release of
the second season of The Witcher in 2021 that,

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:11.480
to better avoid missing a critical character
moment from the novel series in which Geralt

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:15.909
communes with Death, Cavill inserted some
of that dialogue into a different scene.

00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:20.390
Cavill told Digital Spy that he used some
of the novel's dialogue from that scene in

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:24.159
the moment where Geralt deals with the death
of his horse, Roach.

00:03:24.643 --> 00:03:30.000
"Be not afraid of her for she is your friend."

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.712
Cavill told Digital Spy,

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:43.920
Cavill also recently spoke with Looper about
Enola Holmes 2 and admitted that during filming,

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:49.040
he and actress Millie Bobby Brown indulged
in some improvisational work on-set.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.260
He said in the interview,

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.230
Now that's called dedicating yourself to the
art of acting.

